- Unhook it!

1202
01:22:19,018 --> 01:22:20,269
Come on!

1203
01:22:20,645 --> 01:22:21,854
Come on!

1204
01:22:34,659 --> 01:22:37,411
This is Nelec. Use the big guns.

1205
01:22:37,495 --> 01:22:40,373
Whatever happens to me,
do not let it...

1206
01:22:42,208 --> 01:22:43,960
- Joe, open it!
- Open the door!

1207
01:22:44,043 --> 01:22:47,046
- It's bolted!
- I want to go home so bad!

1208
01:22:47,130 --> 01:22:48,589
Open the door.

1209
01:22:48,673 --> 01:22:50,883
- Please, sir.
- Just let us out!

1210
01:22:51,968 --> 01:22:53,177
Please open it!

1211
01:22:53,261 --> 01:22:54,387
Where are the keys?

1212
01:22:54,887 --> 01:22:56,305
Overmyer had them!

1213
01:22:56,389 --> 01:22:58,599
Help me! My leg's stuck!

1214
01:22:58,683 --> 01:23:00,226
Please, sir, open the door!

1215
01:23:00,309 --> 01:23:01,727
Please, open the door!

1216
01:23:06,566 --> 01:23:07,859
Another one dead!

1217
01:23:10,069 --> 01:23:11,779
Guys, there's broken glass.

1218
01:23:11,904 --> 01:23:13,030
Guys!

1219
01:23:13,114 --> 01:23:15,324
Martin! Martin!
Let me get on your shoulders. Come on.

1220
01:23:15,408 --> 01:23:16,492
Go, go, get up!

1221
01:23:16,576 --> 01:23:17,994
- Here we go.
- Go!

1222
01:23:18,077 --> 01:23:20,163
- Come on, Joe! You can do it!
- Come on, Joe!

1223
01:23:20,246 --> 01:23:22,373
- You can do it, Joe! Let's go.
- Come on!

1224
01:23:22,456 --> 01:23:23,875
- Come on!
- You can do it! Come on!

1225
01:23:31,132 --> 01:23:32,967
Joe, please! Go!

1226
01:23:33,384 --> 01:23:36,304
- Come on. Break the glass, you pussy!
- Come on, Joe! Hit it! Come on!

1227
01:23:48,149 --> 01:23:49,442
We got to go!

1228
01:23:56,073 --> 01:23:58,284
- Go!
- Come on, guys, hurry!

1229
01:24:33,319 --> 01:24:36,739
Come with us. We got some questions
for you. Come on.

1230
01:24:36,822 --> 01:24:38,199
- Oh, no. Is she dead?
- Just come with us.

1231
01:24:38,282 --> 01:24:40,743
Hey, fellows,
I've got orders from Colonel Nelec

1232
01:24:40,826 --> 01:24:42,328
to personally deliver this man
back to base.

1233
01:24:42,411 --> 01:24:45,206
- He's all yours, Staff Sergeant.
- Let's go.

1234
01:24:45,289 --> 01:24:48,042
What are you doing?
Where are we going?

1235
01:24:48,626 --> 01:24:49,961
To find our kids.

1236
01:24:53,673 --> 01:24:56,676
Hey, guys! Guys, I found them!

1237
01:24:58,302 --> 01:25:01,097
Hey, guys! I found my firecrackers!

1238
01:25:01,180 --> 01:25:02,181
Congratulations.

1239
01:25:02,265 --> 01:25:06,394
Let's go, guys, they're coming back.
I think we should go. Come on.

1240
01:25:07,436 --> 01:25:08,729
Guys, come on.

1241
01:25:09,730 --> 01:25:11,190
No. No, look.

1242
01:25:15,194 --> 01:25:18,030
You dorks are alive? I thought that...

1243
01:25:20,366 --> 01:25:21,742
What the fuck?

1244
01:25:21,826 --> 01:25:22,994
Donny. Donny.

1245
01:25:23,077 --> 01:25:24,620
We need a ride into town.

1246
01:25:24,704 --> 01:25:28,416
Okay, but just so you know,
I'm massively stoned right now.

1247
01:25:29,041 --> 01:25:31,002
Do you want me to drive?

1248
01:25:34,714 --> 01:25:36,841
- Guys, what was that?
- It sounds like gunshots.

1249
01:25:36,924 --> 01:25:39,302
- Joe, where are we going?
- I saw something in the cemetery.

1250
01:25:39,385 --> 01:25:42,430
Woodward said it was subterranean.
I think I know where it is.

1251
01:25:42,513 --> 01:25:45,224
What the hell is that?
Move the damn car!

1252
01:25:52,565 --> 01:25:54,150
- God!
- Joe, turn the car around!

1253
01:25:54,233 --> 01:25:55,484
- I can't. There's a tank behind us.
- Holy shit!

1254
01:25:55,568 --> 01:25:57,028
- What are they shooting at?
- Guys, we have to run.

1255
01:25:57,111 --> 01:25:58,904
Donny! Hey, Donny, wake up!

1256
01:25:58,988 --> 01:26:01,824
- He's too stoned!
- Drugs are so bad!

1257
01:26:08,331 --> 01:26:10,750
- Why is everyone firing?
- We gotta go!

1258
01:26:11,083 --> 01:26:13,085
Guys, come on, hurry!

1259
01:26:13,169 --> 01:26:15,921
- This is crazy!
- What is going on?

1260
01:26:16,839 --> 01:26:18,424
Look! It just exploded!

1261
01:26:18,758 --> 01:26:22,178
Sir! The weapons are misfiring!
All of them!

1262
01:26:22,261 --> 01:26:25,723
Surface-to-air! Radar!
It's a mess out here, sir!

1263
01:26:27,808 --> 01:26:29,852
Guys! Guys, run!

1264
01:26:30,102 --> 01:26:31,354
Come on!

1265
01:26:31,687 --> 01:26:33,314
What the hell is this?

1266
01:26:33,481 --> 01:26:35,191
Go, Cary, go!

1267
01:26:37,610 --> 01:26:39,153
- Jesus!
- Go!

1268
01:26:43,449 --> 01:26:45,785
What the hell?
Holy shit!

1269
01:26:55,711 --> 01:26:57,755
Why is everyone firing?

1270
01:27:00,299 --> 01:27:02,301
Go, come on!
Move ahead!

1271
01:27:05,471 --> 01:27:06,847
Oh, my God!

1272
01:27:14,772 --> 01:27:16,232
Come on, guys, move!

1273
01:27:16,315 --> 01:27:19,235
Did you guys see those explosions?
They were... They were huge!

1274
01:27:19,985 --> 01:27:21,362
Oh, my God.

1275
01:27:23,531 --> 01:27:24,740
Whose house is this?

1276
01:27:24,824 --> 01:27:27,201
It's Kathy's. I got it off the fridge.

1277
01:27:27,284 --> 01:27:29,412
Kathy? Yeah, I know her.

1278
01:27:30,162 --> 01:27:32,289
Charles, what are you thinking, dude?
That's not yours!

1279
01:27:32,373 --> 01:27:34,417
What, I'm thirsty. I'm in a war zone!

1280
01:27:34,500 --> 01:27:35,918
- Clear! Clear!
- Come on, move!

1281
01:27:36,001 --> 01:27:37,711
Let's go, move out!

1282
01:27:38,337 --> 01:27:40,089
- Guys, come on, let's go.
- Where are we going?

1283
01:27:40,172 --> 01:27:41,549
To the cemetery. I'm...

1284
01:27:47,012 --> 01:27:49,723
Guys, what happened to my leg?
Man, it hurts!

1285
01:27:51,225 --> 01:27:54,520
Holy shit, Martin, you've got
a bone sticking out of your leg!

1286
01:27:55,896 --> 01:27:58,107
Joe, give me that thing off the curtains!

1287
01:27:58,190 --> 01:27:59,358
God!

1288
01:28:00,443 --> 01:28:03,362
I've got to go find Alice.
You guys stay here with Martin.

1289
01:28:03,904 --> 01:28:05,573
You gonna be okay without me?

1290
01:28:06,365 --> 01:28:07,450
Yeah.

1291
01:28:08,200 --> 01:28:11,620
- I'm not staying with the girls!
- God, Cary! Shut up!

1292
01:28:11,704 --> 01:28:13,706
- Calm down!
- Come on! Come on!

1293
01:28:13,789 --> 01:28:15,040
It hurts, Joe!

1294
01:28:15,124 --> 01:28:17,543
Okay, this is going to hurt
really bad, okay?

1295
01:28:18,419 --> 01:28:20,504
Jesus, Martin, I haven't done it yet!

1296
01:28:31,765 --> 01:28:32,975
Just... Just follow me. Just follow me.

1297
01:28:33,058 --> 01:28:36,270
I've been following you for the last five
blocks! What are we doing here?

1298
01:28:36,353 --> 01:28:38,564
Come on, through these doors.
Help me.

1299
01:28:38,647 --> 01:28:41,650
- Help you with what?
- We have to get inside.

1300
01:28:41,734 --> 01:28:43,527
Okay, okay. For what?

1301
01:28:44,445 --> 01:28:45,821
I'll tell you in a second.

1302
01:28:45,905 --> 01:28:48,032
Why is there dirt in these windows?

1303
01:28:51,076 --> 01:28:53,329
It's here. Hard on three.
One, two, three.

1304
01:28:53,412 --> 01:28:55,206
One, two, three!

1305
01:28:55,289 --> 01:28:58,083
- One, two, three! One, two, three!
- One, two, three! One, two, three!

1306
01:29:08,594 --> 01:29:10,429
This... This is scary.

1307
01:29:10,846 --> 01:29:12,264
You got any sparklers in there?

1308
01:29:13,516 --> 01:29:14,517
Are you kidding me?

1309
01:29:26,862 --> 01:29:28,113
Alice is down there.

1310
01:29:43,754 --> 01:29:45,923
I came to your house that day

1311
01:29:46,799 --> 01:29:50,344
to tell you that
I never meant to hurt anyone.

1312
01:29:52,471 --> 01:29:54,056
I swear to God.

1313
01:29:57,226 --> 01:29:58,811
I'm sorry, Jack.

1314
01:30:00,688 --> 01:30:03,107
About what happened to your wife.

1315
01:30:11,949 --> 01:30:13,659
It was an accident.

1316
01:30:21,000 --> 01:30:22,751
It was an accident.

1317
01:30:41,937 --> 01:30:43,731
Joe, I don't understand...

1318
01:30:47,109 --> 01:30:48,402
This way.

1319
01:30:55,951 --> 01:30:59,705
<i>Why are you so surprised?
I always wear lipstick on my shirt.</i>

1320
01:31:44,875 --> 01:31:46,377
- It's Sheriff Pruitt!
- I know.

1321
01:31:46,794 --> 01:31:48,170
Cary, look.

1322
01:31:51,256 --> 01:31:52,883
There are bodies everywhere.

1323
01:31:52,966 --> 01:31:56,178
- What is this?
- We're under the water tower. Look.

1324
01:32:04,895 --> 01:32:07,606
She's got to be here.
She's got to be here.

1325
01:32:20,494 --> 01:32:22,496
It's eating a person.

1326
01:32:27,000 --> 01:32:28,085
She's here.

1327
01:32:28,377 --> 01:32:30,129
Oh, my God. I see her.

1328
01:32:30,546 --> 01:32:33,132
Okay.
We're going to use your firecrackers.

1329
01:32:34,049 --> 01:32:36,176
I don't think that's gonna hurt him, Joe.

1330
01:32:36,260 --> 01:32:38,846
- There's other tunnels.
- So?

1331
01:32:38,929 --> 01:32:41,640
I need you to make noise
right here in two minutes.

1332
01:32:41,724 --> 01:32:44,935
Make it loud and make it last.
Give me some sparklers.

1333
01:32:45,018 --> 01:32:49,356
Make sure you're gone when it blows.
You can't be here. You got to run.

1334
01:32:50,607 --> 01:32:52,359
Where are you going?

1335
01:33:26,935 --> 01:33:28,353
Come on, Cary.

1336
01:34:15,651 --> 01:34:17,694
Alice. Alice. Please, we have to go.
Come on.

1337
01:34:17,778 --> 01:34:19,738
Alice! Alice!

1338
01:34:21,156 --> 01:34:23,116
Please, come on.
We have to go. Alice!

1339
01:34:30,123 --> 01:34:31,959
You're alive! You're alive.

1340
01:34:32,584 --> 01:34:35,254
You're alive. Are you okay?
Can you hear me?

1341
01:34:35,337 --> 01:34:38,340
What is this? What are you doing here?

1342
01:34:38,423 --> 01:34:40,133
I'm just doing the best I can to save you.

1343
01:34:50,185 --> 01:34:51,854
How did you know?

1344
01:34:52,271 --> 01:34:55,691
Your dad. He told me. He was worried.

1345
01:34:55,774 --> 01:34:57,401
And flipping out.

1346
01:34:58,026 --> 01:34:59,486
- Really?
- We have to move.

1347
01:34:59,987 --> 01:35:01,321
Excuse me?

1348
01:35:03,657 --> 01:35:05,117
Where are we?

1349
01:35:06,076 --> 01:35:07,119
I left my bag in the car,

1350
01:35:07,202 --> 01:35:09,121
and then I went out to the car
to get my bag...

1351
01:35:09,204 --> 01:35:10,664
It's been locked up for years.

1352
01:35:10,747 --> 01:35:13,625
It's terrified and hungry
and it just wants to go home.

1353
01:35:13,709 --> 01:35:14,710
When it touched me, I knew.

1354
01:35:14,793 --> 01:35:17,462
I need you to help me
get the Sheriff down.

1355
01:35:28,807 --> 01:35:30,350
Follow me this way.
I'll get us out of here.

1356
01:35:30,434 --> 01:35:32,477
- Sheriff, we came that way.
- Don't argue with me! Just follow me!

1357
01:35:32,561 --> 01:35:34,021
Come on, kids, let's go with the Sheriff.

1358
01:35:45,866 --> 01:35:47,159
This way.

1359
01:35:49,119 --> 01:35:50,329
Joe!

1360
01:35:52,456 --> 01:35:53,749
I told you to get out!
What are you doing here?

1361
01:35:53,832 --> 01:35:56,627
I thought this was the way out.
Okay, I tried.

1362
01:35:56,710 --> 01:35:58,337
- Hey, Alice, welcome back.
- Hey!

1363
01:35:58,420 --> 01:36:00,172
Come on! We got to get out of here...

1364
01:36:02,633 --> 01:36:03,675
Guys, hurry!

1365
01:36:07,304 --> 01:36:08,513
Come on, go!

1366
01:36:12,684 --> 01:36:15,854
She's gone! It took her!
I don't want to be next!

1367
01:36:37,960 --> 01:36:42,130
- Go! You don't want to be here! Go!
- Joe, what are you doing?

1368
01:36:50,305 --> 01:36:52,140
Ally, what the hell is he doing?

1369
01:36:52,224 --> 01:36:53,725
We understand!

1370
01:36:57,562 --> 01:36:58,772
But not everyone's horrible.

1371
01:37:00,232 --> 01:37:01,775
- No!
- Joe!

1372
01:37:03,527 --> 01:37:04,987
Let him down!

1373
01:37:15,080 --> 01:37:17,082
I know bad things happen.

1374
01:37:19,584 --> 01:37:21,253
Bad things happen.

1375
01:37:25,173 --> 01:37:27,092
But you can still live.

1376
01:37:31,555 --> 01:37:32,889
You can still live.

1377
01:38:15,515 --> 01:38:17,309
Okay, wait a minute.

1378
01:38:17,642 --> 01:38:18,810
What?

1379
01:39:06,399 --> 01:39:08,276
- Look out!
- Get down! Get down!

1380
01:39:46,106 --> 01:39:47,566
What is he doing?

1381
01:39:48,733 --> 01:39:50,527
He's making a model.

1382
01:40:35,405 --> 01:40:36,740
I got you.

1383
01:40:38,617 --> 01:40:39,951
I got you.

1384
01:42:28,059 --> 01:42:29,978
Holy shit!

1385
01:44:24,592 --> 01:44:26,261
This is where my friend was attacked.

1386
01:44:26,344 --> 01:44:28,471
- By who?
- I've never seen him before.

1387
01:44:28,763 --> 01:44:32,058
He looked pale, crazy. He bit my friend.

1388
01:44:32,142 --> 01:44:33,560
- Then what happened?
- He was dead.

1389
01:44:33,643 --> 01:44:35,437
- And then...
- He got up and walked away?

1390
01:44:35,520 --> 01:44:37,313
- How did you know?
- Anything left behind?

1391
01:44:37,689 --> 01:44:40,316
Yes, this fell out of the pocket
of the attacker's pocket.

1392
01:44:40,400 --> 01:44:41,484
Thank you.

1393
01:44:44,404 --> 01:44:46,573
Hello, Mr. President.
I'm Detective Hathaway.

1394
01:44:46,656 --> 01:44:50,493
I'm here to discuss some urgent matters
regarding your chemical factory.

1395
01:44:50,577 --> 01:44:52,579
Are you referring
to the recent incidents?

1396
01:44:52,662 --> 01:44:53,663
Yes, I believe I am.

1397
01:44:53,746 --> 01:44:55,123
Tell the chairman I'll call him back.

1398
01:44:55,540 --> 01:44:57,167
You have three minutes.

1399
01:44:57,792 --> 01:45:00,462
You want to tell me
about those employees?

1400
01:45:00,545 --> 01:45:04,007
I was sorry to hear
of their unfortunate accident.

1401
01:45:04,090 --> 01:45:07,343
That was no accident!
Did you see the bites on their neck?

1402
01:45:07,427 --> 01:45:08,928
Are you suggesting some connection

1403
01:45:09,012 --> 01:45:12,515
between my chemical company
and those, those...

1404
01:45:12,599 --> 01:45:14,309
Those were zombie attacks!

1405
01:45:14,517 --> 01:45:17,270
Romero Chemical has nothing to do
with any such thing.

1406
01:45:17,395 --> 01:45:19,022
Then what happens in Building 47?

1407
01:45:19,522 --> 01:45:22,400
You wouldn't mind
if I took a look around, would you?

1408
01:45:23,401 --> 01:45:24,944
Of course not.

1409
01:45:28,698 --> 01:45:30,325
Good day to you, Mr. President.

1410
01:45:30,408 --> 01:45:32,118
Good day, Detective.

1411
01:45:34,370 --> 01:45:35,580
He knows.

1412
01:46:07,946 --> 01:46:09,989
Judith. It's me, your boss.

1413
01:46:10,073 --> 01:46:11,908
I need you to buy my wife
a ticket to Michigan.

1414
01:46:11,991 --> 01:46:15,453
It's too dangerous for her here.
I just love her so much.

1415
01:46:17,622 --> 01:46:20,375
John, I don't like it.
This case. These murders.

1416
01:46:20,458 --> 01:46:22,877
Well, what am I supposed to do,
go to Michigan with you?

1417
01:46:22,961 --> 01:46:25,380
Mackinac Island's beautiful
this time of year.

1418
01:46:25,463 --> 01:46:27,298
Sweetheart, this is my job.

1419
01:46:27,423 --> 01:46:29,259
I just love you so much!

1420
01:46:29,342 --> 01:46:30,635
I love you, too.

1421
01:46:40,270 --> 01:46:42,480
I can't believe
we weren't killed last night.

1422
01:46:42,564 --> 01:46:44,732
Okay, now you have to leave town.

1423
01:46:44,816 --> 01:46:46,651
No. I'm staying here with you.

1424
01:46:46,734 --> 01:46:49,112
I don't know what I would do
if something happened to you.

1425
01:46:49,195 --> 01:46:50,738
What if there are survivors down there?

1426
01:46:50,822 --> 01:46:53,449
There were no survivors!
Did you see that crash?

1427
01:46:53,533 --> 01:46:55,618
Excuse me, sir, were you in the wreck?

1428
01:47:03,167 --> 01:47:05,837
That settles it. I'm not going anywhere.

1429
01:47:08,339 --> 01:47:10,425
It's been two weeks,
and the murders continue.

1430
01:47:10,508 --> 01:47:12,260
This investigation is like no other.

1431
01:47:12,343 --> 01:47:16,180
It's putting too much stress on this town
and on my marriage.

1432
01:47:18,224 --> 01:47:20,101
Could zombies be real?

1433
01:47:22,103 --> 01:47:24,105
Hello? This is Detective Hathaway.

1434
01:47:24,188 --> 01:47:25,898
I'll be right over.

1435
01:47:26,691 --> 01:47:29,110
- What's happening here?
- A military police investigation.

1436
01:47:29,193 --> 01:47:30,486
It was a suicide.

1437
01:47:30,570 --> 01:47:33,698
- A suicide? Who was it?
- A former Air Force officer.

1438
01:47:33,781 --> 01:47:36,034
Said there was a secret
he couldn't keep any longer.

1439
01:47:36,117 --> 01:47:38,077
It says he worked for Dr. Peter Braken?

1440
01:47:38,161 --> 01:47:39,746
I never would have given you
this information

1441
01:47:39,829 --> 01:47:41,372
if we hadn't served together in Vietnam.

1442
01:47:41,873 --> 01:47:44,375
- Those were hard times.
- I'd rather not talk about it.

1443
01:47:47,337 --> 01:47:48,880
- Doctor.
- Detective.

1444
01:47:48,963 --> 01:47:51,090
I'm here to discuss your involvement
with Romero Chemical?

1445
01:47:51,174 --> 01:47:53,593
I was the one that developed
the special compound

1446
01:47:53,676 --> 01:47:55,470
to turn all these humans into zombies.

1447
01:47:55,553 --> 01:47:57,764
It was supposed to be used
as a military weapon,

1448
01:47:57,847 --> 01:47:59,974
but it got out of hand.
So I made this antidote

1449
01:48:00,058 --> 01:48:02,644
that will hopefully cure
all of the zombies.

1450
01:48:02,727 --> 01:48:04,479
That's incredible!
How much have you made?

1451
01:48:04,937 --> 01:48:06,522
Just this one.

1452
01:48:06,606 --> 01:48:10,735
Would you like to help me test it
on this innocent victim of my creation?

1453
01:48:32,298 --> 01:48:33,633
Honey, I'm home!

1454
01:48:33,716 --> 01:48:37,053
Good news. We found a cure
for the zombie infection.

1455
01:48:37,136 --> 01:48:38,304
Honey?

1456
01:48:59,701 --> 01:49:03,037
Sorry. It didn't work. I wish it worked.

1457
01:49:03,287 --> 01:49:05,957
I tried. I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

1458
01:49:07,625 --> 01:49:08,626
John?

1459
01:49:23,641 --> 01:49:26,436
This has been
a Charles Kaznyk production.

1460
01:49:27,145 --> 01:49:30,481
We had such a fun time filming
this movie, <i>The Case.</i>

1461
01:49:30,982 --> 01:49:33,651
So much fun that I hope you pick it

1462
01:49:33,735 --> 01:49:37,155
for the Cleveland International
Super 8 Film Festival.

1463
01:49:37,780 --> 01:49:38,781
God!

